---
// HeroShowcase — the above-the-fold app preview on the homepage.
//
// Desktop (>= 820px): a browser-framed desktop view (Piggy Bank Overview) with
// two phones in front (Family Nook + Calendar) — the "works on your laptop AND
// your phone" story.
// Mobile (< 820px): a swipe carousel of the five core app screens with dots and
// gentle autoplay, so the hero stays short and the CTA stays high.
//
// Every screen is a pure-CSS render (NO images) so it adds no LCP/CLS weight —
// the same reason the previous showcase was CSS. All classes are namespaced with
// `hsx-` (or scoped under `.hsx`) because the marketing site defines global
// `.card`, `.tag`, `.btn-primary` etc. The <style> is `is:global`, NOT Astro-
// scoped, on purpose: the cluster/carousel/scaleboxes/dots are created in JS, and
// Astro scoped styles only reach server-rendered elements — the hsx- prefix is
// what keeps it collision-safe.
//
// Screens are pre-rendered once into a hidden pool and MOVED (never cloned) into
// the cluster or carousel by the inline script. Content is illustrative (fake
// demo family), mirrors the real app's layout, and is aria-hidden.
---

<div class="hsx" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="hsx-stage" data-hsx-stage>
    <button class="hsx-arrow hsx-arrow--prev" type="button" data-hsx-prev aria-label="Show previous screens">‹</button>
    <div class="hsx-inner" data-hsx-inner>
      <div class="hsx-anchor hsx-anchor--d" data-hsx-ad></div>
      <div class="hsx-anchor hsx-anchor--a" data-hsx-aa></div>
      <div class="hsx-anchor hsx-anchor--b" data-hsx-ab></div>
    </div>
    <button class="hsx-arrow hsx-arrow--next" type="button" data-hsx-next aria-label="Show more screens">›</button>
  </div>
  <div class="hsx-dots" data-hsx-dots></div>

  <!-- Pre-rendered screen pool (hidden; nodes are moved into place by script) -->
